# JIT differential skip list for the trap-diagnostics fixture corpus.
#
# One entry per line:  <fixture-name>: <reason>
#
# A listed fixture still runs on the interpreter; only the JIT pass is
# skipped. An entry is justified only when the JIT cannot compile the
# fixture at all (never because its trace disagrees — a disagreement is a
# bug the corpus exists to catch). Entries naming unknown fixtures, and
# fixtures that fail under the JIT without an entry, fail the runner.
#
# Currently empty: every fixture in the corpus compiles and runs under the
# JIT on the targets probed when the corpus was added (Linux x86_64).
